{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head 4d5d9c2d91ef1ce023aa41728645d834b3d97a87. I examined the reporting artifact first and all 12 companion artifacts. The scope is request #24993, including the requester's condition-2 clarification in #25043.\n\nThree repairs are required.\n\n1. P1 — Own the signed bytes behind the verified dedup index. At internal/kernel/kernel.go@4d5d9c2d91ef1ce023aa41728645d834b3d97a87, eventWithoutPayload retains the returned event's Signed buffers, and PriorActsAt returns those buffers again. NewSubmitterFrom clones the map but still shares its values' buffers. TestReviewReaderKeepsVerifiedSignedBytesPrivate changes the Signed bytes returned by PriorActsAt to another valid intent under the same key. ReplayAt then answers replay=true, held=true, err=nil, where it must report the idempotency conflict. TestReviewSeededWorldIgnoresEditsToReturnedLoadEvents makes the same edit through Reader.Load's returned events; the seeded Submitter likewise replays the changed intent at the old commit. Both tests compile and fail with -race at this exact head. Protect the verified index at ingress and at the new lookup's return boundary, and add regression tests for both paths. Cloning only the lookup result leaves the Load-to-seeded-submitter path exposed.\n\n2. P1 — Own the nested vocabulary slices before lending a snapshot. At internal/workroom/kinds.go@4d5d9c2d91ef1ce023aa41728645d834b3d97a87, sortedDefinitions copies Fields and Basis only one level deep. Fields[].Values and Basis[].Kinds still share storage with the folder. The new sessionFoldAt path therefore renders a supposedly private admission world from state a snapshot caller can edit. TestReviewAdmissionDoesNotInheritCallerVocabularyEdits changes a returned Basis.Kinds entry; admission's vocabulary then differs from a cold audit at the same head. TestReviewAdmissionDoesNotInheritCallerFieldValues first adopts a constrained custom kind and reproduces the same defect through Fields.Values. Both compile and fail with -race here. This new reuse makes the existing shallow getter an admission trust boundary. Protect both nested slices and pin both cases with tests whose missing copies go red.\n\n3. P2 — Complete the measurement report required by condition 1. The reporting artifact lists selected wall times and one aggregate local memory figure. It omits the full before/after wall-time and peak-RSS matrix for ratify, state, one-path artifact and review-request on both local and resident routes. The raw bench2.log already contains those routes; bench3.log confirms three final cases. Publish the complete table, label accepted and refused cases, and identify the measured binary heads, frozen frontier and retained raw evidence. Keep the report's attribution of old measurements separate from any confirmation at the repaired head. Also update the final paragraph's task status: faster-fold request d1b3d1b1d8a481ad0bda38d7b137764e0a3a28d3 is already landed in the measured main baseline.\n\nArchitecture: layers 2, 4 and 5 change their process-local reuse contract, and docs/reference/architecture.md is updated and published in this artifact set. It records the private consume-only reader, reader-frontier gate, checkpoint cadence, scratch-fold limit and periodic seeded-cache rebuild. The intended change fits the bounded implementation request. Findings 1 and 2 prevent the implementation from meeting its documented private-world and verified-index ownership contract.\n\nSecurity: findings 1 and 2 remain unresolved. A current head and a previously successful audit do not make caller-shared mutable buffers trustworthy. The reproductions violate the conflicting-retry and caller-independent admission conditions without forging an actor signature.\n\nSimplification: use the existing cloneSigned helper at the ownership boundaries and independently copy the two nested constraint slices. These narrow controls resolve the reproduced defects within the existing request and promise.\n\nValidation: the four ownership probes fail at the unmodified published head. The own-append lookup probe passes. Independently, TestSigningCommandsVerifyTheLogOnce and TestSigningCommandRefusesATamperedCheckpoint pass together with -race (7.811 s). In a disposable copy, the two signed-byte boundary copies and two nested vocabulary copies make all five reviewer probes pass with -race (kernel 1.787 s; app 3.660 s). Both modified source files were then restored byte-for-byte to the published head. The author's full-5.log passes across the suite; I read that log and the bench2/bench3 raw samples, and did not independently rerun the full suite or timing campaign.\n\nCurrent-head raw logs are /tmp/gitseq-world-4d5d-kernel-ownership.log, /tmp/gitseq-world-4d5d-app-ownership.log, /tmp/gitseq-world-4d5d-ownership-copy-control.log and /tmp/gitseq-world-4d5d-command-gates.log. The reproducer source and earlier control results are embedded durably in git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8457239bd0e4c586f2887673bc194cf7ee73fea5. The additional custom-field probe is /private/tmp/gitseq-world-review-4d5d-iwpcclip/internal/app/zz_review_field_values_test.go.\n\nRepair on the same implementation request and promise, publish every changed path including the ownership repair, and request exact-head review again.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:83ccd285b70002a7d214cc63ee8ee889e7a103d3","binding":"assigned","head":"4d5d9c2d91ef1ce023aa41728645d834b3d97a87","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f13dfde17822e71317ad798a10a27a4a16ba9036\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6635856f91f679e1970abb6a544a8dd01a6ffa61\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:f13dfde17822e71317ad798a10a27a4a16ba9036","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}